    "done_when": "The the-suite-is-green-at-head followup f-sgh-discovery-memo-leaks-across-tests holds. Every test that changes reckon.serve._SIGNATURE_TTL_S restores it after the test, through monkeypatch or an autouse fixture, so no later test in the same process sees a memo it did not set. The candidates are tests/test_discovery_reads_each_file_once.py and tests/test_rollup_reuses_watched_walks.py, and the manifest names which one left it at 60.0 and how. A new test, tests/test_discovery_memo_does_not_leak.py, runs the leaking test file and tests/test_server_listens_before_it_watches.py in one child pytest process, without xdist, in that order. It asserts the entry-point test passes. A declared negative control is executed and logged under pytest: removing the restore turns the new test red with the \"discovery memo live\" message. The node gate is the new test file plus tests/test_server_listens_before_it_watches.py, tests/test_discovery_reads_each_file_once.py and tests/test_rollup_reuses_watched_walks.py at head, ending EXIT=0. Every log sits under the run directory, headed with revision, tree and literal command, and ends EXIT=. Only tests/test_discovery_reads_each_file_once.py, tests/test_rollup_reuses_watched_walks.py, tests/conftest.py (only if an autouse fixture is the fix) and the new test file change.",
